# Russian sayings: без труда́…
subtitle: "Five Russian sayings, word by word: what each one means and when to say it, from без труда́ to у́тро ве́чера мудрене́е."
tags: ["russian","russian proverbs","russian sayings","без труда","russian culture"]
teaches: ["vocabulary/sayings"]
thumb: "band \"Even the fish takes work\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"A whole conversation in Russian","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/99-russian-conversation.cast"}

## Russian sayings: без труда́…
